    `git rebase main` takes the commits from the current branch (the feature branch) that are not in `main` and applies them one by one onto the tip of `main`.
    
    If the feature branch has 3 commits, `git rebase main` will attempt to apply each of these 3 commits onto the new base.
    
    For each commit being applied, a conflict can occur.
    If each commit introduces changes that conflict with the current state of the rebased branch, you could encounter a conflict for each commit.
    
    So, if there are 3 commits, you could encounter conflicts at most 3 times.
    
